    "body": "Happy Wednesday, everyone! I hope you have a warm drink ready because today's Pips puzzle was a cozy one. I started with the Easy mode, and my eyes immediately jumped to that massive sum region in the middle. Seeing a target of 25 for just five cells meant I needed to use some of the biggest faces available. Since the domino [5,5] takes up two of those spots at [2,2] and [2,3], that already gave me 10 points. I then looked for other dominoes with 5s and 6s to fill out the rest of that area.\n\nThe real trick to finishing this one was the equals constraint over on the left side between [1,0] and [2,0]. By looking at the dominoes I had left, I realized that [5,2] and [2,3] could both provide a 2 for those cells. Once I placed the 5 from the [5,2] domino into the sum region at [1,1], everything else just clicked into place. I ended up putting the [5,6] domino at [1,4] and [1,3], which satisfied the less than 3 rule for the single cell at [1,4] too. It is always so satisfying when the last piece fits perfectly!",
