    "body": "The Medium puzzle today felt like a step up in logic, mostly because of how the equals constraints were chained together. I spent a good few minutes staring at the bottom right corner. We had an equals rule for [2,3] and [3,3], and another one for [3,1] and [3,2]. This essentially created a path I had to follow. I found that starting with the sum of 13 at the bottom left was the way to go. To get to 13 using cells [2,0], [2,1], and [2,2], I had to use two 6s and a 1.\n\nOnce I knew [2,1] was a 6 and [2,2] was a 1, the rest of the dominoes started falling like, well, dominoes! The [6,4] domino fit perfectly at [3,1] and [2,1], which then told me that [3,2] had to be a 4 to match the equals constraint. The greater than 4 constraint at cell [1,4] was also a big help. It restricted that cell to being either a 5 or a 6, which helped me narrow down which of the remaining high-value dominoes went in the upper-right section. It was a fun little brain teaser that required looking a few steps ahead.",
