    "body": "Wow, Rodolfo Kurchan really outdid themselves with this Hard puzzle! Instead of big regions, we had a grid where every single cell had its own sum target. It felt like a mix between a crossword and a jigsaw puzzle. Since each cell target represents the pips on that specific half of a domino, I started by hunting for all the zeros. There were quite a few scattered around at [0,3], [1,1], [1,5], [2,5], and [4,3]. Knowing those had to be the blank side of a domino gave me some great anchors to work from.\n\nFrom there, it was all about matching the pairs. For example, [0,0] needed 2 pips and [0,1] needed 4 pips, so I just had to find the [2,4] domino and lay it across those two cells. The most challenging part was keeping track of which dominoes I had already used. I hit a small snag near the bottom right when I mixed up where the [3,5] and [4,5] dominoes went, but once I realized cell [4,5] specifically needed 5 pips, it cleared right up. If you take it cell by cell and cross off the dominoes as you go, this one is a very rewarding solve!",
